{"graph_chars": "Good morning. I am Professor Hana Park. This lecture is Chapter Three of Principles of Macroeconomics, OpenStax, third edition: Demand and Supply. The opening case is organic food. An organic Fuji apple costs two dollars seventy-five a pound. A conventional one costs one dollar seventy-two. If organic is often local, why is it not cheaper? The same model that prices gasoline will answer that. In June two thousand twenty, a gallon of gas in the United States averaged three dollars sixteen. By January two thousand twenty-one it was two dollars forty-two. Economists do not judge those prices. They ask what buyers are willing to pay and what sellers are willing to accept. This chapter is one of the most powerful models in all of economics: demand, supply, equilibrium, then what happens when the curves shift, when government sets a ceiling or a floor, and whether the result is efficient.", "graph_times": [[0.0, 0.0637], [0.0637, 0.1274], [0.1274, 0.1911], [0.1911, 0.2547], [0.2547, 0.3184], [0.3184, 0.3821], [0.3821, 0.4458], [0.4458, 0.5095], [0.5095, 0.5732], [0.5732, 0.6369], [0.6369, 0.7006], [0.7006, 0.7642], [0.7642, 0.8279], [0.8279, 0.8916], [0.8916, 0.9553], [0.9553, 1.019], [1.019, 1.0827], [1.0827, 1.1464], [1.1464, 1.2101], [1.2101, 1.2737], [1.2737, 1.3374], [1.3374, 1.4011], [1.4011, 1.4648], [1.4648, 1.5285], [1.5285, 1.5922], [1.5922, 1.6559], [1.6559, 1.7196], [1.7196, 1.7832], [1.7832, 1.8469], [1.8469, 1.9106], [1.9106, 1.9743], [1.9743, 2.038], [2.038, 2.1017], [2.1017, 2.1654], [2.1654, 2.2291], [2.2291, 2.2927], [2.2927, 2.3564], [2.3564, 2.4201], [2.4201, 2.4838], [2.4838, 2.5475], [2.5475, 2.6112], [2.6112, 2.6749], [2.6749, 2.7385], [2.7385, 2.8022], [2.8022, 2.8659], [2.8659, 2.9296], [2.9296, 2.9933], [2.9933, 3.057], [3.057, 3.1207], [3.1207, 3.1844], [3.1844, 3.248], [3.248, 3.3117], [3.3117, 3.3754], [3.3754, 3.4391], [3.4391, 3.5028], [3.5028, 3.5665], [3.5665, 3.6302], [3.6302, 3.6939], [3.6939, 3.7575], [3.7575, 3.8212], 